Subject: harden ipo_paper_ledger RLS to match ipo_corpus_examples

PREPARED, NOT APPLIED. Phase B is engine-only; this is staged for whoever runs
the paper-environment phase.

Apply with:
    git apply docs/patches/ipo_paper_ledger_rls.patch

The migration 20260921120000 is still UNAPPLIED, so this is an edit to a pending
file, not a schema change to a live database.

WHY EACH LINE IS NEEDED

  FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY
    ENABLE alone does not constrain the table OWNER. Without FORCE, a query run
    as the owning role reads every row regardless of policy. ipo_corpus_examples
    (migration 20260920100000) already sets it; this table did not.

  REVOKE ALL FROM anon, authenticated
    RLS governs rows; GRANTs govern reachability. Leaving default grants in
    place means PostgREST will attempt the query and rely on RLS to refuse it.
    Revoking makes the table unreachable rather than merely empty.

  GRANT ALL TO service_role
    Explicit rather than inherited, so the edge function keeps working if
    default privileges change.

--- a/supabase/migrations/20260921120000_ipo_paper_ledger.sql
+++ b/supabase/migrations/20260921120000_ipo_paper_ledger.sql
@@
--- Project-owned research data, same posture as the IPO corpus: no anon or
--- authenticated policy. Reachable only with the service role, which means only
--- from the edge function. RLS on with zero policies denies everyone else.
+-- Project-owned research data, matching the posture already established for
+-- ipo_corpus_examples (migration 20260920100000) exactly.
+--
+-- FORCE matters and ENABLE alone is not enough: without it the table OWNER
+-- bypasses RLS, so a query run as the owning role would still read the table.
+-- REVOKE matters too — RLS governs rows, grants govern reachability, and
+-- leaving the default grants in place means PostgREST will happily attempt the
+-- query before RLS refuses it. Both, or the guarantee is partial.
 alter table public.ipo_paper_ledger enable row level security;
+alter table public.ipo_paper_ledger force row level security;
+
+revoke all on public.ipo_paper_ledger from anon, authenticated;
+grant all on public.ipo_paper_ledger to service_role;
